# Copy to .env (git-ignored) in the project or a parent folder, or export these in your shell.
#
# Quoting: use SINGLE quotes for Windows paths. In double quotes a backslash starts an escape
# sequence, so the whole file fails to load (the client then prints a warning and ignores it).

# Path to the Godot executable. Official Windows builds are portable, version-named files, so set
# it explicitly. If it is unset, `GODOT` and then `godot` on PATH are tried.
# Windows: 'C:\Program Files\Godot\Godot_v4.5-stable_win64.exe'
# Linux:   "/usr/bin/godot"
# macOS:   "/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot"
GODOT_PATH=

# Feedback to the maintainers (see "Reporting problems with the bridge" in the README):
# full (default), draft (reports only, never submitted) or off.
# DEV_BRIDGE_FEEDBACK=full
# The GitHub CLI to submit reports with, when it is not `gh` on PATH.
# DEV_BRIDGE_GH=
